  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5090",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to LOUCY through a series of molecular interactions. The first pathway links Mollicellin N to A704, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and then to LOUCY. The second pathway connects Mollicellin N to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a compound that also targets LOUCY. The third pathway links Mollicellin N to TE-9, which is targeted by the same compound that targets LOUCY. These pathways suggest that Mollicellin N may act through different molecular mechanisms, but all ultimately converge on LOUCY as a downstream target. The evidence supports a potential role for Mollicellin N in modulating LOUCY through various receptor or enzyme pathways, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
